    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1069">

                <pb facs="1160" n="1064" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1064"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-03-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 2, 1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 288.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 272, of the
                    23d ultimo, I have the honor to inclose herewith two letters which have appeared
                    in the Times, one from the pen of Sir E. J. Reed, late chief constructor of <pb
                        facs="1161" n="1065" xml:id="pg1065"/> the British navy, with respect to the
                    raising of the <hi rendition="#italic">Maine;</hi> also a letter of condolence
                    from the president of the Glasgow Chamber of Commerce and Manufactures, for
                    which I duly thanked him.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1069-a1.xml" xpointer="d1069-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
